From 387ab7437d10209b5dbf3d1c420c87c13b18518f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:37:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] test(shader): results served from the disk cache match
 the compile

disk_cache_hit_tests compiles two compute shaders (a waterfall loop and a
branch between table slots) through the caches with a fresh disk cache,
then runs itself again: that process must load every resource plan,
variant and specialized module from disk, specialize nothing, and give the
same SPIR-V, bindings and push data, which also match a compile without
caches. It also checks HashSpirvWords2 against HashSpirvWords under both
seeds and ContentHash, and that a resource plan decoded from its encoding
encodes to the same bytes (and a truncated one is refused).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
